# Cloudflare Pages response headers (copied to dist/ by scripts/build.mjs).
#
# Pages, scripts and styles are checked with the server on every visit
# (Cache-Control: no-cache): the browser and Cloudflare may keep a copy, but
# ask first whether it changed, so a new deploy shows up on the next load and
# an unchanged file costs a quick "304 Not Modified". This is what keeps the
# owner dashboard (/admin/) and the planner from running last week's code.
#
# Not listed: /api/*. Pages Functions set their own headers and _headers never
# applies to them. Images, fonts and icons keep Cloudflare's defaults. The
# service worker (sw.js) keeps its own copy of the planner for offline use and
# goes to the network first, so the installed app still opens offline.
#
# One rule per address: when two rules match, Pages joins their values, so
# the page addresses below are exact and every file is covered by its type.
# tests/cache-headers.test.js checks that every page and file of the site is matched once.
#
# The old addresses of the Teams and partners pages (1.30) are redirects
# (_redirects); Pages adds the headers of a matching rule to a redirect too.
# no-store: none of these redirects is ever kept by a browser.
# Until 1.29, /teams and /partners redirected the other way, permanently, to
# exactly /welcome/teams/ and /welcome/partners/, and browsers keep a
# permanent redirect for good: someone who opened /teams then would bounce
# between /teams/ and /welcome/teams/ for ever. Clear-Site-Data "cache" on
# those two exact addresses empties this site's HTTP cache as they answer, so
# the kept redirect is gone; it never touches the planner's data
# (localStorage, IndexedDB, the offline copy: that would be "storage").
# Only there (they take no-store from /welcome/teams/* and /welcome/partners/*:
# different headers, nothing joined): the browser goes through its whole HTTP cache
# first, half a second or more when it is large, and this site's files are
# then downloaded again, so the other old addresses (/welcome/teams, deeper
# links) only get no-store. Rules match the path, never the query, so
# /welcome/teams/?ask=question pays it too; 1.28 kept the query, so
# /teams/?ask=question went there and may be a kept redirect as well.
# 2026-10-21: remove the two Clear-Site-Data rules in a release after
# 2027-01-31. By then browsers have dropped those old redirects (or come
# through here once and lost them), while each visit to an old address
# would still pay for the scan.

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/admin/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/teams/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/partners/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/welcome/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/welcome/thanks/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/legal/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/legal/privacy/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/legal/terms/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/legal/cookies/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/welcome/teams
  Cache-Control: no-store
/welcome/teams/*
  Cache-Control: no-store
/welcome/partners
  Cache-Control: no-store
/welcome/partners/*
  Cache-Control: no-store
/welcome/teams/
  Clear-Site-Data: "cache"
/welcome/partners/
  Clear-Site-Data: "cache"
